1
00:00:11,000 --> 00:00:15,999
First of all, for making me a witness to the apparition of our Blessed Mother,

2
00:00:16,000 --> 00:00:20,999
I offer a thousand thanks to our Blessed Mother and her Divine Son.

3
00:00:21,000 --> 00:00:28,999
My name is Rani, and this is my husband, Raju, and we belong to St. Joseph's Parish in Chirakkal.

4
00:00:29,000 --> 00:00:33,999
I made the Covenant in 2022.

5
00:00:34,000 --> 00:00:37,999
I am sharing this testimony on behalf of my husband.

6
00:00:38,000 --> 00:00:43,999
My husband used to experience frequent chest pains and shortness of breath.

7
00:00:44,000 --> 00:00:52,999
As he was having a lot of difficulty, we went to the hospital and did an angiogram test.

8
00:00:53,000 --> 00:01:01,999
After the tests, the doctor advised an angiogram, and it revealed a 90% block.

9
00:01:02,000 --> 00:01:05,999
They strongly recommended a bypass surgery.

10
00:01:06,000 --> 00:01:12,999
Since my husband was not willing to undergo a bypass surgery, we asked for an angioplasty, but the doctor refused.

11
00:01:13,000 --> 00:01:20,999
He said there was no point in doing that and a bypass was strictly necessary, so we went to another hospital.

12
00:01:21,000 --> 00:01:27,999
When we consulted the doctor there, he said an angioplasty could be done despite some risks.

13
00:01:28,000 --> 00:01:35,999
He agreed to do the angioplasty, and thus, on August 4th, the procedure began.

14
00:01:36,000 --> 00:01:40,999
Right in the middle of the angioplasty procedure, he suffered a massive heart attack.

15
00:01:41,000 --> 00:01:48,999
The heart attack made his condition extremely critical, and time stood still.

16
00:01:49,000 --> 00:01:53,999
When they finally brought my husband out of the theater, he had no breath left in him.

17
00:01:54,000 --> 00:01:58,999
His eyes were barely open, and he looked completely lifeless.

18
00:01:59,000 --> 00:02:04,999
They brought him out in a highly critical state, and I desperately asked the doctor what had happened.

19
00:02:05,000 --> 00:02:10,999
The doctor explained that a heart attack occurred during the angioplasty, and his condition was dire.

20
00:02:11,000 --> 00:02:18,999
He was being moved to a ventilator, and my husband slightly opened his eyes and just looked at me.

21
00:02:19,000 --> 00:02:25,999
The doctors rushed him to the ventilator, and after about half an hour, the doctor came out.

22
00:02:26,000 --> 00:02:33,999
He told us his condition was extremely critical, saying, "We have done everything we can; there is nothing more left in our hands."

23
00:02:34,000 --> 00:02:43,999
His BP had dropped drastically, his heart's pumping was very weak, and all his vital organs had almost failed.

24
00:02:44,000 --> 00:02:50,999
He was 99% clinically dead, and they told me I could go in and see him if I wanted to.

25
00:02:51,000 --> 00:02:59,999
When I went inside, his eyes were covered with cotton, his mouth was slightly open, and he laid there stiff.

26
00:03:00,000 --> 00:03:05,999
He looked almost exactly like a corpse, and I could only bear to take one look at him.

27
00:03:06,000 --> 00:03:10,999
The doctor kept saying things, but I couldn't even pay attention, so I quickly went back to our room.

28
00:03:11,000 --> 00:03:17,999
My younger brother, his daughter, and my elder sister were with me, and my brother asked what went wrong.

29
00:03:18,000 --> 00:03:24,999
He said, "He went in looking so calm, what happened all of a sudden?", to which the doctor explained about the massive heart attack.

30
00:03:25,000 --> 00:03:31,999
The doctor said there was no hope of survival, as he was completely unresponsive and surrounded entirely by life-support machines.

31
00:03:32,000 --> 00:03:35,999
He was only being kept alive by those machines.

32
00:03:36,000 --> 00:03:41,999
They said they had done everything they possibly could, while many doctors surrounded him, trying various procedures.

33
00:03:42,000 --> 00:03:47,999
After about an hour had passed, they advised us to inform all our relatives.

34
00:03:48,000 --> 00:03:54,999
They are nine siblings in total, and when everyone arrived, the doctor told them there was no hope left.

35
00:03:55,000 --> 00:04:03,999
He said they would take him off the ventilator by 10 AM the next day, and told us to prepare to take the body. There's no more hope, they said.

36
00:04:04,000 --> 00:04:10,999
I immediately called my sister's son and daughter-in-law and told them, "I need to go to Kreupasanam in the morning."

37
00:04:11,000 --> 00:04:16,999
I told them I must go and pray at the feet of our Blessed Mother, and they arrived early, around 6 AM.

38
00:04:17,000 --> 00:04:23,999
My nephew, his wife, and I came straight to Kreupasanam, entering the presence of our Blessed Mother.

39
00:04:24,000 --> 00:04:32,999
I went straight to the feet of our Blessed Mother and prayed, "I have come to beg for my husband's life."

40
00:04:33,000 --> 00:04:40,999
That was all I said; I didn't utter another word, but simply looked at Mother and wept bitterly.

41
00:04:41,000 --> 00:04:46,999
My sister's daughter-in-law was standing right next to me, and a phone call came from the hospital.

42
00:04:47,000 --> 00:04:52,999
I knew instantly it was from them, and I stood near her but didn't ask anything.

43
00:04:53,000 --> 00:04:58,999
Only after the call did she speak to me, bearing all her sorrow to break the news.

44
00:04:59,000 --> 00:05:06,999
She told me, "The call was from the doctor; his condition has completely collapsed, and the BP is entirely down."

45
00:05:07,000 --> 00:05:13,999
He was absolutely not responding to any medications, and all his organs were shutting down.

46
00:05:14,000 --> 00:05:22,999
They said there is nothing more to say or do, though she didn't reveal the whole severity to me immediately.

47
00:05:23,000 --> 00:05:30,999
Afterwards, I told her, "Let us go inside the center and pray," so we went inside to pray.

48
00:05:31,000 --> 00:05:36,999
While my niece and I were sitting inside and praying for about 10 or 20 minutes, another phone call came.

49
00:05:37,000 --> 00:05:43,999
She walked over to me and said, "Aunty, Uncle opened his eyes!"

50
00:05:44,000 --> 00:05:51,999
She excitedly said, "His BP has become normal, and the heart's pumping has significantly improved."

51
00:05:52,000 --> 00:05:57,999
He had started responding to the medicines, opened his eyes, and looked around for everyone, surely looking for me.

52
00:05:58,000 --> 00:06:02,999
Everyone was asking me to come back quickly, but even then, I stayed a little longer.

53
00:06:03,000 --> 00:06:10,999
I stayed to offer my heartfelt thanks to our Blessed Mother before we went back to the hospital.

54
00:06:11,000 --> 00:06:16,999
By the time we got there, my husband opened his eyes and looked at me, leaving everyone utterly amazed.

55
00:06:17,000 --> 00:06:22,999
They all asked me, "Even in such a dire moment, you rushed to our Blessed Mother; how could she not hear that prayer?"

56
00:06:23,000 --> 00:06:30,999
They said, "If it were us facing such an agony, we would have just stayed glued to the hospital, but you ran to Mother."

57
00:06:31,000 --> 00:06:37,999
My husband was looking visibly well, and whenever I went in to see him.

58
00:06:38,000 --> 00:06:43,999
I would anoint his forehead with Mother's oil and hold the blessed medal in my hands.

59
00:06:44,000 --> 00:06:48,999
I would place it in his hands and pray over him, always bringing a small statue of our Blessed Mother with me.

60
00:06:49,000 --> 00:06:54,999
The assistant doctor there noticed me constantly praying.

61
00:06:55,000 --> 00:06:58,999
He took the statue and placed it on a stand right above my husband's head.

62
00:06:59,000 --> 00:07:04,999
While my husband was still on the ventilator, the doctor placed it on the stand and told the nurse to stick it there permanently.

63
00:07:05,000 --> 00:07:10,999
He said, "It's a small statue, let Mother's blessing always be upon him; don't bring it back and forth every day, let it stay right here."

64
00:07:11,000 --> 00:07:17,999
And so they kept it there, and he remained on the ventilator for nearly three weeks.

65
00:07:18,000 --> 00:07:24,999
He was then shifted to the ICU, and a week later to a normal room, and now, by the grace of God, he is perfectly fine.

66
00:07:25,000 --> 00:07:29,999
He is completely healed, and though he takes his medications, he has absolutely no other issues.

67
00:07:30,000 --> 00:07:34,999
We actively buy newsletters for others, gives food to people, and helps the poor.

68
00:07:35,000 --> 00:07:39,999
After all this, the doctors had predicted that I would only be able to walk with support even after six months.

69
00:07:40,000 --> 00:07:45,999
Now six months have passed, and God has granted me the strength to walk completely independently.

70
00:07:46,000 --> 00:07:52,999
For this, I offer my profound thanks to God and Blessed Mother. And after a week, we came to visit Fr. Joseph here.

71
00:07:53,000 --> 00:08:01,999
He took a photo of my husband, touched it to the Blessed Mother's statue, and blessed it with the sign of the cross.

72
00:08:02,000 --> 00:08:10,999
He declared that he would recover very soon. For all these showers of blessings, a thousand thanks to God and our Mother!

73
00:08:11,000 --> 00:08:20,999
A reading from the Holy Gospel according to Saint Luke 7:13 "And when the Lord saw her, he had compassion on her and said to her, 'Do not weep.'"

74
00:08:21,000 --> 00:08:26,999
"Then he came up and touched the bier, and the bearers stood still."

75
00:08:27,000 --> 00:08:34,999
"And he said, 'Young man, I say to you, arise.' And the dead man sat up and began to speak, and Jesus gave him to his mother."

76
00:08:35,000 --> 00:08:45,999
Rani's husband Raju, a man who was 99% clinically dead, is standing before us at this altar as a living witness to the apparition.

77
00:08:46,000 --> 00:08:52,999
It was when all hope was lost that Rani left her husband on the ventilator,

78
00:08:53,000 --> 00:09:00,999
and ran into the presence of our Blessed Mother, crying out, "Please restore my husband's life!"

79
00:09:01,000 --> 00:09:07,999
With nothing else to say, in an overwhelming agony where words failed her intercession, Rani sat here,

80
00:09:08,000 --> 00:09:16,999
weeping and praying; and when we look into the Gospels, we encounter many individuals whom Jesus raised from the dead.

81
00:09:17,000 --> 00:09:23,999
We see Jesus raising Lazarus, and Jesus weeping in compassion for their sorrows.

82
00:09:24,000 --> 00:09:31,999
Similarly, in the Old Testament, in the 37th chapter of the Prophet Ezekiel, in the valley of dry bones, God asks the prophet a question.

83
00:09:32,000 --> 00:09:37,999
God asks the Prophet Ezekiel: "Son of man, can these bones live?"

84
00:09:38,000 --> 00:09:44,999
The prophet answered, "O Lord God, you know," for it is something only God, only Jesus, truly knows.

85
00:09:45,000 --> 00:09:48,999
He alone knows whether we will enter into eternal life or not.

86
00:09:49,000 --> 00:09:57,999
To help us enter into eternal life, the great prayer plan and way of life given to us through our Blessed Mother is the Covenant.

87
00:09:58,000 --> 00:10:04,999
Rani and Raju came here, entered into the Covenant, and lived it without losing faith or abandoning hope.

88
00:10:05,000 --> 00:10:10,999
This is the living testimony of reaping a hundredfold harvest of their faithful prayer.

89
00:10:11,000 --> 00:10:19,999
To Jesus and our Blessed Mother, for this immense grace and the mighty blessing of restoring him to life, let us offer our thanks and lift up this testimony with a resounding round of applause.

90
00:10:20,000 --> 00:10:32,999
Extraordinary divine experiences can now be yours too. If you haven't subscribed to this YouTube channel yet, please subscribe right now.

91
00:10:33,000 --> 00:10:37,000
Share this video with your friends right now, and become missionaries of the Lord.
